From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] _CStdlib.h: skip libstdc++-trap headers under Swift C++
 importer

When Swift's Clang importer parses _FoundationCShims in C++ interop mode
(-cxx-interoperability-mode=default / swift-6, or a target using
.interoperabilityMode(.Cxx)), <math.h>, <tgmath.h> and <complex.h> resolve
to libstdc++'s C++ wrappers at usr/include/c++/<ver>/{math,tgmath,complex}.h.
Those wrappers include <cmath>/<ccomplex>/<ctgmath>, which reference headers
in libstdc++'s bits/ tree that are members of the `std` Clang module
(see swift's libstdcxx.modulemap at usr/lib/swift/linux/). Clang then
transitively builds the `std` module, whose header list includes <random>,
<bits/random.tcc> fails to compile ("call to 'abs' is ambiguous" between
the C stdlib.h abs(int) and libstdc++'s std_abs.h abs(long) -- no
abs(double) overload is in scope when __CORRECT_ISO_CPP_MATH_H_PROTO
isn't set, which glibc >= 2.38 no longer defines).

Gate the three math-family C headers off when __swift__ && __cplusplus.
The Swift-visible surface is unaffected: on Linux the math entry points
are already imported via Glibc, and the C++ interop importer pass does
not need to re-import them from _FoundationCShims -- it only needs the
rest of the shim (filemanager/string/io/bplist/CFUniChar/target
conditionals). Ordinary C compiles of _CStdlib.h (including Swift
imports without C++ interop) are unaffected, so the C-mode Swift view
of _FoundationCShims keeps its math symbols.

__swift__ is defined by Swift's Clang importer only (see
swift/lib/ClangImporter/ClangImporter.cpp, which calls
languageVersion.preprocessorDefinition("__swift__", ...)), so no
non-Swift consumer of this header sees the skip.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE/Yocto-specific workaround until Swift
upstream teaches the Clang importer's C++ mode to not transitively build
the libstdcxx `std` module for C-shim imports, or until libstdc++'s
math wrappers stop tripping on glibc 2.38+'s removal of
__CORRECT_ISO_CPP_MATH_H_PROTO.]

Signed-off-by: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
---
 Sources/_FoundationCShims/include/_CStdlib.h | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Sources/_FoundationCShims/include/_CStdlib.h b/Sources/_FoundationCShims/include/_CStdlib.h
--- a/Sources/_FoundationCShims/include/_CStdlib.h
+++ b/Sources/_FoundationCShims/include/_CStdlib.h
@@ -51,9 +51,16 @@
 #include <locale.h>
 #endif

+// Swift's Clang importer in C++ interop mode resolves <math.h>, <tgmath.h>
+// and <complex.h> to libstdc++'s C++ wrappers, which transitively force
+// Clang to build the `std` module (libstdcxx.modulemap) and fail in
+// <bits/random.tcc>. Skip these headers only in that pass. Pure-C compiles
+// and C-mode Swift imports are unaffected.
+#if !(defined(__swift__) && defined(__cplusplus))
 #if __has_include(<math.h>)
 #include <math.h>
 #endif
+#endif

 #if __has_include(<signal.h>)
 /// Guard against including `signal.h` on WASI. The `signal.h` header file
@@ -106,10 +113,12 @@
 #endif

 #if !defined(_WIN32)
+#if !(defined(__swift__) && defined(__cplusplus))
 #if __has_include(<tgmath.h>)
 #include <tgmath.h>
 #endif
 #endif
+#endif

 #if __has_include(<time.h>)
 #include <time.h>
@@ -124,9 +133,11 @@
 #endif


+#if !(defined(__swift__) && defined(__cplusplus))
 #if __has_include(<complex.h>)
 #include <complex.h>
 #endif
+#endif

 #if __has_include(<threads.h>)
 #include <threads.h>
--
2.43.0
